go test ./config/ -run TestReproGRPCLevel -v 2>&1 | tail -30. The patch satisfies all three requirements. `LogConfig` gains `GRPCLevel string` with JSON tag `grpc_level` (verified at config/config.go:35-40); `Default()` sets `GRPCLevel: "ERROR"` unconditionally (line ~236); `Load()` reads `log.grpc_level` via `viper.IsSet`/`GetString` (lines ~371-374), matching the existing log-key handling pattern; `Level`, `File`, `Encoding` definitions are unchanged. The self-authored reproduction on the current tree confirmed: default="ERROR", explicit config value populated, omitted value defaults to "ERROR" while other log fields remain intact.

